1
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,390
Alright now! You all fresh niggers,

2
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:14,590
you'all gonna be in the cutting game.

3
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:17,460
Very simple! I want you to take your knife,

4
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:21,600
yank 'em cane, make 'em sing.

5
00:01:21,830 --> 00:01:22,960
Take the cane off.

6
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:27,640
Cut my tops, clean the stalks off.

7
00:01:27,740 --> 00:01:31,190
Throw it on the pile for replanting again.

8
00:01:31,290 --> 00:01:34,010
Now them cane ain't gonna jump up and bite you,

9
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:34,980
don't shy 'bout it.

10
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:37,150
Rushy boys, rushy!

11
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:12,140
Alright, alright, alright.

12
00:07:14,190 --> 00:07:15,310
Thank you for the music.

13
00:07:15,630 --> 00:07:16,280
Come on.

14
00:07:16,470 --> 00:07:17,610
Get in there, boy.

15
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:19,360
Come on.

16
00:07:19,940 --> 00:07:20,700
Give me a kiss.

17
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:28,840
- I love you. - I love you too, dad.

18
00:07:28,940 --> 00:07:30,240
Sleep well.

19
00:07:32,290 --> 00:07:35,090
I'll take this.

20
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:39,240
I don't wanna hear any more noise.

21
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:44,140
Good night.

22
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:52,540
Three weeks and two days.

23
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,840
It is the custom.

24
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:57,990
I wonder what you'll do without me?

25
00:07:58,090 --> 00:07:59,850
I won't stay idle.

26
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:04,190
Darling, it's good money.

27
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:09,320
If only I didn't have to share your cooking with other people.

28
00:08:10,590 --> 00:08:13,390
You don't.

29
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:17,790
Come on.

30
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,290
Be good for your mother.

31
00:08:19,390 --> 00:08:20,880
Ok, Alonzo?

32
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:24,990
Can I get a kiss, please? Thank you.

33
00:08:25,090 --> 00:08:27,440
- Travel safely, love. - Stay safely.

34
00:08:31,090 --> 00:08:33,040
Ready.

35
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:44,680
- Good day, Mr. Northup. - Good day.

36
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:49,440
Call the devil's name. There he is now.

37
00:08:49,540 --> 00:08:50,970
Mr. Northup,

38
00:08:50,980 --> 00:08:53,790
I have two gentlemen acquaintance you should make.

39
00:08:53,890 --> 00:08:56,090
Misters Brown and Hamilton.

40
00:08:56,190 --> 00:08:57,240
Sir.

41
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,200
Mr. Northup, these two gentlemen

42
00:08:59,200 --> 00:09:01,940
were inquiring about distinguished individuals,

43
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:05,140
and I was just this very moment saying Solomon Northup

44
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:07,740
- is an expert player on the violin. - He was indeed.

45
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:09,640
Mr. Moon is being overly gracious.

46
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:12,740
Taking into consideration his graciousness and your modesty,

47
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:15,890
may we trouble you for a moment of your time to converse, sir?

48
00:09:15,990 --> 00:09:17,540
Of course.

49
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:19,040
Sir.

50
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:21,440
- A circus? - That is our usual employee.

51
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:23,240
The company currently in the city of Washington.

52
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,490
Circus too constricting a word to describe

53
00:09:25,590 --> 00:09:27,740
the talented and merry band with which we travel.

54
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:30,840
It is a spectacle unlike most have ever witnessed.

55
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:34,420
Creatures from the darkest Africa as yet unseen by civilized man.

56
00:09:34,630 --> 00:09:36,460
Acrobats from the Orient

57
00:09:36,470 --> 00:09:39,490
who contort themselves in the most confounding manners.

58
00:09:39,590 --> 00:09:41,330
And I myself in aide of Mr. Brown,

59
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:43,390
an internationally renowned practitioner

60
00:09:43,490 --> 00:09:44,990
in the art of prestidigitation.

61
00:09:45,090 --> 00:09:46,890
We are on our way thither to rejoin the company,

62
00:09:46,990 --> 00:09:48,270
having left for a short time

63
00:09:48,270 --> 00:09:50,090
to make a small profit from our own exhibitions.

64
00:09:50,250 --> 00:09:52,470
The reason for our inquiry with Mr. Moon...

65
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:53,770
Yes. We had just a devil of a time

66
00:09:53,770 --> 00:09:55,830
in procuring music for our entertainments.

67
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,970
Men of true talents are seemingly in short supply.

68
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:58,810
Thank you, sir.

69
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:02,190
If we could persuade you to accompany us as far as Washington,

70
00:10:02,290 --> 00:10:04,790
we could give you one dollar for each day's services

71
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:07,240
and three dollars for every night played at our performances.

72
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:09,190
In addition, we would provide sufficient pay,

73
00:10:09,210 --> 00:10:11,260
for your return here to Saratoga,

74
00:10:11,340 --> 00:10:13,420
two weeks from today.

75
00:10:17,750 --> 00:10:20,130
Welcome to Washington, Solomon.

76
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,550
Good Day.

77
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:31,220
- I'm telling you it's too much. - Some say not enough.

78
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,240
Solomon.

79
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:35,590
Forty-three dollars. All to you.

80
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:38,690
That it's far more than my wages amount to.

81
00:10:38,790 --> 00:10:40,640
- To our most profitable week. - Cheers!

82
00:10:40,740 --> 00:10:42,950
- Cheers! - Cheers!

83
00:10:47,390 --> 00:10:48,560
Another.

84
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:54,390
Gentlemen, your generosity

85
00:10:54,490 --> 00:10:57,790
- is extraordinary. - And your talents are undeniable.

86
00:10:57,890 --> 00:11:00,240
- To Solomon! - Cheers.

87
00:11:00,340 --> 00:11:01,710
Cheers.

88
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:46,790
That's all right, Solomon.

89
00:11:46,890 --> 00:11:50,390
No shame in it. No shame at all.

90
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:14,040
Hamilton, we must hurry.

91
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:17,430
One too many libations, have we there?

92
00:12:33,790 --> 00:12:35,560
I'm so sorry.

93
00:12:36,490 --> 00:12:38,340
We won't hear it. We won't.

94
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:41,290
Let him sleep, Hamilton.

95
00:12:41,390 --> 00:12:43,440
A good night's rest.

96
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:46,140
And tomorrow...

97
00:12:46,340 --> 00:12:49,040
Tomorrow you will feel as well and refreshed..

98
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:51,040
as if the earth were new again.

99
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:54,020
Hamilton! There's nothing more we can do for him.

100
00:12:55,690 --> 00:12:57,580
Such is the pity.

101
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:09,700
Well, boy, how yah feel now?

102
00:13:11,740 --> 00:13:13,340
My name...

103
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,690
My name is Solomon Northup.

104
00:13:15,790 --> 00:13:16,840
I am a free man.

105
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,240
a resident of Saratoga, New York.

106
00:13:19,290 --> 00:13:21,840
The residence of my wife and children who are equally free.

107
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:23,990
and you have no right whatsoever to detain me--

108
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,990
- Yah not any free man . - And I promise you,

109
00:13:27,090 --> 00:13:28,920
I promise you upon my liberation

110
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:32,040
I will have satisfaction for this wrong.

111
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:36,630
Resolve this. Produce your papers.

112
00:13:44,490 --> 00:13:46,790
Yah no free man.

113
00:13:46,890 --> 00:13:49,290
And yah ain't from Saratoga.

114
00:13:49,390 --> 00:13:52,390
Yah from Georgia.

115
00:13:54,890 --> 00:13:57,890
Yah ain't a free man.

116
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:03,540
Yah nuthin' but a Georgia runaway.

117
00:14:04,490 --> 00:14:06,390
Yah a just a..

118
00:14:06,490 --> 00:14:11,430
runaway nigger from Georgia.

119
00:14:42,740 --> 00:14:44,790
You're a slave!

120
00:14:44,890 --> 00:14:48,390
Yah a Georgia slave!

121
00:15:04,340 --> 00:15:07,140
Are yah a slave?

122
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:09,740
No.

123
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,070
Help!

124
00:16:09,190 --> 00:16:11,690
Help me!

125
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:14,740
Help me!

126
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:17,060
Somebody help me!

127
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:19,940
Help!

128
00:16:22,230 --> 00:16:23,500
Help!

129
00:16:34,990 --> 00:16:37,990
That old thing of yours is just rags and tatters.

130
00:16:38,090 --> 00:16:40,240
You need something proper to wear.

131
00:16:43,490 --> 00:16:46,490
Go'on. Put it on.

132
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:06,620
There.

133
00:17:10,330 --> 00:17:11,590
That's fine.

134
00:17:12,220 --> 00:17:13,810
That's fine.

135
00:17:16,210 --> 00:17:17,560
Got no gratitude?

136
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:25,940
- No! It was from my wife. - Rags and tatters.

137
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:27,660
Rags and tatters.

138
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:39,520
Go on. Warsh up.

139
00:17:42,630 --> 00:17:44,340
The boy, too. Get him clean.

140
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:48,940
Scrub now.

141
00:17:49,040 --> 00:17:50,470
Do you know when my mama will come?

142
00:17:51,890 --> 00:17:53,790
- Hush him up! - Mama! Mama!

143
00:17:53,890 --> 00:17:56,650
- Quiet! Quiet. Quiet! - Mama!

144
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,090
- Hush him up! - Mama!

145
00:17:58,140 --> 00:18:00,040
Your mother will come, I swear she will,

146
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,940
but you must be silent.

147
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:04,440
Be silent!

148
00:18:10,230 --> 00:18:11,990
We need a sympathetic ear.

149
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:14,800
An opportunity to explain our situation--

150
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,940
Who in your estimation is that sympathetic ear?

151
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:18,680
The two men I journeyed with.

152
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,240
I'm certain they're making inquires at this very moment.

153
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:22,780
I would be just as certain they are counting the money

154
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:23,910
paid for delivering you to this place.

155
00:18:23,990 --> 00:18:26,440
They were not kidnappers. They were artists.

156
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:28,790
- Fellow performers. - You know that?

157
00:18:28,890 --> 00:18:31,030
You know for certain who they were?

158
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:35,970
The reality to come is us being transported southward.

159
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,590
New Orleans if I was to venture.

160
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:42,190
After we arrive, we'll be put to market.

161
00:18:42,290 --> 00:18:43,620
And beyond that...

162
00:18:44,890 --> 00:18:47,590
well, I suppose once in a slave state there's only one outcome.

163
00:18:47,690 --> 00:18:48,190
No.

164
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:50,210
I don't say that to give you empty agitation, John...

165
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:52,560
For y'all. For y'all they ain't nothin' but that!

166
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:53,760
But John was'n kidnapped.

167
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:56,340
John is bein' hold as debt, tha's all.

168
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:58,340
Massa pay his debt, and John be redeemed--

169
00:18:58,440 --> 00:18:59,910
Boy, our masters will not come for us.

170
00:18:59,910 --> 00:19:02,130
John... John's sorry for y'all, but tha's how it be.

171
00:19:02,130 --> 00:19:04,220
Where y'all goin', yah goin' witout John.

172
00:19:06,190 --> 00:19:08,840
- Mama! - Randall.

173
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:10,100
Mama!

174
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:14,340
Are you alright?

175
00:19:21,100 --> 00:19:23,040
Come on, get up!

176
00:19:23,140 --> 00:19:24,840
- I said get up! - No, no, don't...

177
00:19:24,890 --> 00:19:27,040
Now, I don't want to hear yer talk. Get in the yard.

178
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,490
- No, I'm not sure... - Ain't no need for all that.

179
00:19:29,590 --> 00:19:32,040
Just take a little trip, that's all.

180
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:33,420
Don't want to frighten the children

181
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:35,590
over a little boat ride, do yah?

182
00:19:35,690 --> 00:19:37,680
John's massa gunna pay his debt.

183
00:19:38,340 --> 00:19:39,720
His massa gunna pay his debt.

184
00:19:45,540 --> 00:19:48,030
I don't want to hear a word, out of none a yah.

185
00:19:48,990 --> 00:19:50,200
Not a one.

186
00:20:02,290 --> 00:20:03,690
No!

187
00:20:03,790 --> 00:20:06,290
All right, come on.

188
00:20:07,590 --> 00:20:08,470
Come on!

189
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:11,270
Come on, child, come on.

190
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,470
Follw your mom.

191
00:20:13,860 --> 00:20:14,980
- Come on, boy. - Come on.

192
00:20:18,640 --> 00:20:20,340
Come on, move it!

193
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:22,590
Let's go! Come on! Up, upstairs.

194
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:24,440
Hit it!

195
00:20:24,540 --> 00:20:25,740
Come on, let's go.

196
00:20:28,440 --> 00:20:30,590
Get up there, kid!

197
00:20:30,690 --> 00:20:32,240
Come on, move it!

198
00:20:32,340 --> 00:20:34,540
- All right, come on! - Move it, boy!

199
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:35,790
Take him down!

200
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:38,340
Hey, you! Come on, get up!

201
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:41,440
Get down, right there.

202
00:20:42,590 --> 00:20:43,310
Come on.

203
00:20:45,290 --> 00:20:46,750
Right there. Sit down.

204
00:21:23,140 --> 00:21:25,470
Cheer up and don't be so cast down.

205
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:39,660
If you want to survive, do and say as little as possible.

206
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:42,940
Tell no one who you really are,

207
00:21:42,940 --> 00:21:45,540
and tell no one you can read and write.

208
00:21:47,490 --> 00:21:49,620
Unless you want to be a dead nigger.

209
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:08,070
Now, keep your mouth shut.

210
00:22:15,340 --> 00:22:17,990
I say we fight.

211
00:22:18,090 --> 00:22:20,340
The crew is fairly small.

212
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,260
If it were well planned,

213
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:22,790
I believe they could be strong armed.

214
00:22:22,790 --> 00:22:25,740
Three can't go against a whole crew?

215
00:22:25,840 --> 00:22:28,140
The rest here are niggers,

216
00:22:28,240 --> 00:22:31,990
born and bred slaves. Niggers ain't got no stomach for a fight.

217
00:22:32,090 --> 00:22:35,390
- Not a damn one. - All I know,

218
00:22:35,490 --> 00:22:39,240
we get where we're travelling, we'll wish we'd died right here.

219
00:22:39,340 --> 00:22:41,990
Survival is not about certain death,

220
00:22:41,990 --> 00:22:44,490
it is about keeping your head down.

221
00:22:47,390 --> 00:22:51,390
Days ago I was with my family,

222
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:53,580
in my home.

223
00:22:55,140 --> 00:22:57,290
Now you tell me all is lost.

224
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:02,840
Tell no one who I am? That's the way to survive.

225
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:07,920
Well, I don't want to survive.

226
00:23:09,690 --> 00:23:12,390
I want to live.

227
00:24:41,340 --> 00:24:45,960
It's better off. Better than us.

228
00:25:02,490 --> 00:25:05,040
I don't see him. Clemens!

229
00:25:05,140 --> 00:25:07,140
Clemens Ray!

230
00:25:07,240 --> 00:25:09,440
- Clemens! - Master Ray, sir!

231
00:25:09,540 --> 00:25:11,740
- Who's in charge here? - I'm the captain!

232
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:13,290
I am Mr. Jonas Ray.

233
00:25:13,390 --> 00:25:16,250
My solicitor has documentation verifying

234
00:25:16,250 --> 00:25:17,740
that the Negro known as Clemens Ray is my property.

235
00:25:17,840 --> 00:25:20,290
I know nothing of this arrangement.

236
00:25:20,950 --> 00:25:23,020
You are ordered to return that property immediately

237
00:25:23,050 --> 00:25:25,260
or be charged with thievery.

238
00:25:25,700 --> 00:25:28,140
Free him!

239
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:33,240
Master!

240
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:36,240
Clemens! Clemens!

241
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,540
- Get back! Get him back! - Clemens!

242
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:40,390
Clemens!

243
00:25:40,490 --> 00:25:41,650
Clemens!

244
00:26:48,150 --> 00:26:49,140
Mr. Parker?

245
00:26:49,580 --> 00:26:51,280
Oh, Mr. Northup.

246
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:52,580
Mrs. Northup,

247
00:26:53,090 --> 00:26:55,340
Solomon, can I interest you with a new cravat?

248
00:26:55,340 --> 00:26:56,660
Pure silk by way of the French.

249
00:26:56,660 --> 00:26:59,020
We are in need of a fresh carry all for my Mrs's travels.

250
00:26:59,020 --> 00:26:59,890
Nothing more.

251
00:26:59,990 --> 00:27:03,040
A year's passed already? Off towards Sandy Hill again?

252
00:27:03,140 --> 00:27:05,490
- Yes , I am. - I have just the thing.

253
00:27:06,340 --> 00:27:08,090
Something to suit your style,

254
00:27:08,090 --> 00:27:09,960
and yet sturdy enough for the forty miles round trip.

255
00:27:10,040 --> 00:27:12,380
- It's beautiful. - But at what price?

256
00:27:12,590 --> 00:27:13,460
We will take it.

257
00:27:13,670 --> 00:27:16,910
Children, come see what your father has just purchased for me.

258
00:27:17,330 --> 00:27:18,860
One moment, sir, and you will be assisted.

259
00:27:18,860 --> 00:27:20,090
- Mr. Parker? - Sir?

260
00:27:20,190 --> 00:27:22,110
If we can discuss the price...

261
00:27:22,110 --> 00:27:24,190
Forgive me, Solomon, Mrs. Northup.

262
00:27:24,190 --> 00:27:24,990
A customer waits.

263
00:27:24,990 --> 00:27:26,290
Welcome, sir.

264
00:27:26,290 --> 00:27:28,060
Shop well sir, but mind your wallet.

265
00:27:28,060 --> 00:27:31,170
- Pay no attention to this gentleman's nonsense. - Jasper!

266
00:27:32,090 --> 00:27:34,660
My regrets for the intrusion, sir.

267
00:27:34,660 --> 00:27:36,990
No intrusion.

268
00:27:39,740 --> 00:27:42,790
- Good day, sir. - Good day.

269
00:27:42,890 --> 00:27:45,390
Jasper, out!

270
00:27:52,890 --> 00:27:55,390
Very good.

271
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:58,180
Let's see here... Eliza!

272
00:27:59,340 --> 00:28:02,440
Stand up when you hear your name. Eliza?

273
00:28:03,120 --> 00:28:04,080
Lethe!

274
00:28:07,590 --> 00:28:08,310
John!

275
00:28:10,040 --> 00:28:10,820
Oren.

276
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,480
Platt!

277
00:28:16,530 --> 00:28:17,510
Platt!

278
00:28:20,980 --> 00:28:22,140
Stand up.

279
00:28:24,030 --> 00:28:27,030
You fit the description given. Why didn't you answer when called?

280
00:28:27,130 --> 00:28:29,340
My name is not Platt. My name is...

281
00:28:31,780 --> 00:28:33,260
Your name is Platt.

282
00:28:35,730 --> 00:28:38,180
Captain, get these niggers to my cart.

283
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:06,160
I believe I have something

284
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:08,180
very much your liking in the back room.

285
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:10,180
Follow me, please.

286
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:11,880
Yes. Now...

287
00:29:11,980 --> 00:29:14,280
Inspect them at your leisure, but ...

288
00:29:14,380 --> 00:29:18,030
I ask you to pay particular regard to young Ezra right here.

289
00:29:18,130 --> 00:29:19,790
Incredibly solid limbs!

290
00:29:19,790 --> 00:29:21,780
I've never seen anything quite like him.

291
00:29:21,880 --> 00:29:24,830
And this marvelous creature. Can you believe it? Hm?

292
00:29:24,950 --> 00:29:26,960
She'd make a fine living maids, mandam.

293
00:29:28,230 --> 00:29:30,930
So, inspect at your leisure. Take your time.

294
00:29:30,930 --> 00:29:32,380
Help yourself to refreshments.

295
00:29:32,430 --> 00:29:35,180
Gentlemen, what catches your fancy here?

296
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:36,930
Hm... this boy?

297
00:29:37,030 --> 00:29:39,380
Open your mouth. Open, wide up!

298
00:29:39,480 --> 00:29:41,980
Look in there. Never been sick a day in his life.

299
00:29:41,980 --> 00:29:43,970
And I call particular attention to Martha.

300
00:29:43,970 --> 00:29:45,840
She is an excellent pastry cook.

301
00:29:45,980 --> 00:29:47,520
Ah, Mr. Ford?

302
00:29:48,670 --> 00:29:51,230
Splendid seeing you, sir. What catches your fancy?

303
00:29:51,230 --> 00:29:52,780
This lad, he's very browny.

304
00:29:53,100 --> 00:29:56,630
How much for the ones Platt and Eliza?

305
00:29:56,730 --> 00:29:57,610
Ah, I see...

306
00:29:57,610 --> 00:30:02,520
A thousand for Platt, he is a nigger of considerable talent.

307
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:03,220
I assure you.

308
00:30:03,230 --> 00:30:04,980
Seven hundred for Eliza.

309
00:30:04,980 --> 00:30:06,440
My fairest price.

310
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:10,440
- You would accept a note? - Please, sir...

311
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:11,510
Of course, from you, Mr. Ford.

312
00:30:11,760 --> 00:30:12,920
Please sir, don't divide my family.

313
00:30:13,110 --> 00:30:13,690
Don't take me

314
00:30:13,850 --> 00:30:15,370
- unless you take my children as well. - Eliza, quiet!

315
00:30:15,650 --> 00:30:17,360
You will have the most faithful slave in me.

316
00:30:17,510 --> 00:30:18,960
The most faithful slave that has ever lived,

317
00:30:19,170 --> 00:30:20,270
- but I beg that you do not separate us. - Your price

318
00:30:20,450 --> 00:30:21,550
- for the boy? - Yes, the boy.

319
00:30:22,180 --> 00:30:23,260
- Please! - Stop it!

320
00:30:23,260 --> 00:30:24,550
I will give you something to cry about.

321
00:30:24,550 --> 00:30:26,930
Randall, come forward. Come, come, come.

322
00:30:26,930 --> 00:30:28,630
You see how fit this boy is.

323
00:30:29,630 --> 00:30:30,810
Like ripe fruit.

324
00:30:30,810 --> 00:30:32,790
May I take your stick, for a moment?

325
00:30:33,140 --> 00:30:35,050
Observe this, Randall?

326
00:30:35,050 --> 00:30:35,740
Jump, jump, jump! Run, run, run!

327
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:38,240
Very good! Higher!

328
00:30:38,240 --> 00:30:43,090
You see this? Very likely he will grow into a fine beast.

329
00:30:43,970 --> 00:30:46,190
Six hundred for the boy,

330
00:30:46,290 --> 00:30:47,480
fair and final.

331
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:50,690
- Done. - Superb.

332
00:30:50,790 --> 00:30:52,290
A moment, please.

333
00:30:52,390 --> 00:30:54,390
- Mr. Ford? - Please.

334
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:56,580
- Eliza! - How much for the little girl?

335
00:30:58,490 --> 00:30:59,540
You have no use for her.

336
00:30:59,550 --> 00:31:01,840
One so young will bring you no profit.

337
00:31:01,890 --> 00:31:03,640
No, no, no, no. I cannot sell the girl.

338
00:31:03,740 --> 00:31:07,390
- Please! - There's heaps 'n piles of money to be made for her.

339
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:09,790
She is a beauty. One of the regular bloods.

340
00:31:09,890 --> 00:31:11,360
None of your thick-lipped, bullet headed,

341
00:31:11,360 --> 00:31:12,840
cotton picking niggers.

342
00:31:12,890 --> 00:31:16,390
- Her child, man. - Please...

343
00:31:16,790 --> 00:31:18,890
For God's sake, are you not sentimental in the least?

344
00:31:18,940 --> 00:31:22,490
My sentimentality extends the length of a coin.

345
00:31:23,940 --> 00:31:27,340
Now do you take this lot, Mr. Ford, or do you pass on them all?

346
00:31:27,440 --> 00:31:30,940
Please, please ...

347
00:31:31,140 --> 00:31:32,840
I will take the ones Platt and Eliza.

348
00:31:32,890 --> 00:31:34,560
So, Eliza and Platt, splendid.

349
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:35,960
I will not go without my children.

350
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:38,760
You will not take them from me.

351
00:31:38,760 --> 00:31:39,760
Goddamn! Get her out!

352
00:31:39,760 --> 00:31:40,760
Please! No!

353
00:31:41,390 --> 00:31:45,990
No, no, no...!

354
00:31:50,990 --> 00:31:53,240
Get her out of here! Out! Out! Out!

355
00:31:57,210 --> 00:31:58,020
Nice.

356
00:31:59,990 --> 00:32:01,990
Mr Ford, pleasure.

357
00:32:18,940 --> 00:32:21,290
Did you bring all those niggers?

358
00:32:21,390 --> 00:32:22,740
Two of them?

359
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:25,840
- You got two? - Mr. Chapin.

360
00:32:25,940 --> 00:32:28,490
This one's cryin'. Why is this one cryin'?

361
00:32:28,590 --> 00:32:30,890
- Separated from her children. - Oh, dear...

362
00:32:30,990 --> 00:32:33,340
- It couldn't be helped. - Poor, poor woman.

363
00:32:33,440 --> 00:32:34,690
- Mr. Chapin. - Yes , sir.

364
00:32:34,790 --> 00:32:36,590
Tomorrow you will take these two up to the mill

365
00:32:36,590 --> 00:32:37,940
and start them workin'.

366
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:39,190
For now make them adequate,

367
00:32:39,220 --> 00:32:41,290
fix them a meal, and have them rest themselves.

368
00:32:41,340 --> 00:32:43,390
Yes, sir.

369
00:32:43,490 --> 00:32:47,540
C'mon, now. C'mon. Don't dawdle.

370
00:32:47,640 --> 00:32:50,380
Something to eat and some rest;

371
00:32:50,400 --> 00:32:52,170
your children will soon enough be forgotten.

372
00:33:18,910 --> 00:33:21,510
For all of you rotten niggers that don't know,

373
00:33:21,510 --> 00:33:23,190
My name is John Tibeats,

374
00:33:23,290 --> 00:33:25,990
William Ford's chief carpenter.

375
00:33:26,090 --> 00:33:29,490
You will refer to me as Master.

376
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:33,390
Now, Mister Chapin is the overseer on this plantation,

377
00:33:33,440 --> 00:33:36,490
and you too will refer to him

378
00:33:36,590 --> 00:33:38,120
as Master.

379
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:40,640
So, clap your hands.

380
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:45,390
Like this.

381
00:33:46,390 --> 00:33:48,790
Come on. Come on now.

382
00:33:48,890 --> 00:33:49,790
Clap your hands.

383
00:33:54,490 --> 00:33:56,740
Nigger run nigger flew.

384
00:33:56,840 --> 00:33:59,340
Nigger tore his shirt in two.

385
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:01,740
Run run the pattyroller will get you.

386
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:05,840
Run nigger run well you better get away

387
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:10,590
That's right. Like you mean it.

388
00:34:11,490 --> 00:34:13,740
Nigger run, run so fast

389
00:34:13,840 --> 00:34:16,140
Stoved his head in a hornets nest

390
00:34:16,240 --> 00:34:18,590
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

391
00:34:18,690 --> 00:34:21,150
Run nigger run well you better get away

392
00:34:21,990 --> 00:34:24,390
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

393
00:34:24,490 --> 00:34:27,190
Run nigger run well you better get away

394
00:34:28,790 --> 00:34:30,840
Some folks say a nigger won't steal

395
00:34:30,890 --> 00:34:33,190
I caught three in my corn field

396
00:34:33,290 --> 00:34:35,490
One has a bushel and one has a peck

397
00:34:35,590 --> 00:34:37,940
One had a rope and it was hung around his neck

398
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:40,390
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

399
00:34:40,490 --> 00:34:42,890
Run nigger run well you better get away

400
00:34:42,990 --> 00:34:45,290
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

401
00:34:45,390 --> 00:34:47,840
Run nigger run well you better get away

402
00:34:48,140 --> 00:34:50,690
Hey Mr. Pattyroller don't catch me

403
00:34:50,790 --> 00:34:53,090
Catch that nigger behind that tree

404
00:34:53,190 --> 00:34:55,590
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

405
00:34:55,690 --> 00:34:57,890
Run nigger run well you better get away

406
00:34:57,990 --> 00:35:00,240
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

407
00:35:00,340 --> 00:35:02,140
Run nigger run well you better get away

408
00:35:02,400 --> 00:35:04,540
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

409
00:35:04,770 --> 00:35:06,950
Run nigger run well you better get away

410
00:35:07,490 --> 00:35:09,710
I am the God of Abraham,

411
00:35:09,710 --> 00:35:13,690
and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.

412
00:35:14,240 --> 00:35:16,630
And when the multitude heard this,

413
00:35:16,630 --> 00:35:19,240
they were astonished at his doctrine.

414
00:35:19,440 --> 00:35:22,340
Then one of them, which was a lawyer,

415
00:35:22,440 --> 00:35:25,890
asked him a question, tempting him.

416
00:35:25,890 --> 00:35:27,890
Run nigger run well the pattyroller will get you

417
00:35:27,890 --> 00:35:30,890
Run nigger run well you better get away

418
00:36:21,690 --> 00:36:24,390
The creek is plenty deep enough to sail,

419
00:36:24,490 --> 00:36:26,690
even with a boat full of load.

420
00:36:26,790 --> 00:36:29,140
The distance from the work area to the point on the latter bayou

421
00:36:29,190 --> 00:36:31,140
is several miles by water fewer than land.

422
00:36:31,190 --> 00:36:32,380
It occurs to me that

423
00:36:32,380 --> 00:36:34,390
the expense of the transportation would be materially diminished.

424
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:37,240
- "Materially diminished?" - If we use the waterway.

425
00:36:37,790 --> 00:36:40,330
Are you an engineer or a nigger?

426
00:36:42,890 --> 00:36:45,270
Are you an engineer or a nigger?

427
00:36:46,690 --> 00:36:49,090
- Let the man say his piece. - It's a scheme.

428
00:36:49,190 --> 00:36:51,460
Plenty of engineers have schemed similarly.

429
00:36:51,680 --> 00:36:53,670
The passes are too tight.

430
00:36:54,590 --> 00:36:57,840
I reckon them at more than twelve feet at their most narrow.

431
00:36:57,940 --> 00:36:59,490
Wide enough for a tub to traverse,

432
00:36:59,490 --> 00:37:01,090
if a team of niggers cleared it out.

433
00:37:01,190 --> 00:37:03,890
And you know what of transport and terra formin'?

434
00:37:03,990 --> 00:37:06,290
I labored repairing the Champlain canal,

435
00:37:06,340 --> 00:37:07,470
on the section over which

436
00:37:07,470 --> 00:37:09,290
William Van Nortwick was superintendent.

437
00:37:09,390 --> 00:37:12,340
With my earnings I hired several efficient hands to assist me,

438
00:37:12,440 --> 00:37:13,610
and entered into contracts for

439
00:37:13,610 --> 00:37:15,290
the transportation of large rafts of timber

440
00:37:15,390 --> 00:37:17,700
from Lake Champlain to Troy.

441
00:37:20,340 --> 00:37:23,250
I'll admit to being impressed even if you won't.

442
00:37:24,640 --> 00:37:27,130
Collect a team, see what good you can do.

443
00:37:35,790 --> 00:37:37,040
All right, you're good. Clear it up!

444
00:37:37,250 --> 00:37:39,110
One, two, three...

445
00:38:09,970 --> 00:38:11,650
Platt, you are a marvel.

446
00:38:19,910 --> 00:38:20,990
What took you so long?

447
00:38:22,230 --> 00:38:23,220
Thank you, Master Ford.

448
00:38:23,220 --> 00:38:24,060
No, thank you.

449
00:38:25,100 --> 00:38:26,620
- Yeah! - Hi, Model!

450
00:38:26,820 --> 00:38:27,720
Yes, sir!

451
00:38:41,840 --> 00:38:42,610
Platt.

452
00:39:02,110 --> 00:39:04,410
My great thanks, Master Ford.

453
00:39:04,650 --> 00:39:06,010
My thanks to you,

454
00:39:06,860 --> 00:39:08,260
and it is the least of it.

455
00:39:09,380 --> 00:39:12,300
My hope is that it brings us both much joy over the years.

456
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:50,090
Eliza.

457
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:56,510
Eliza.

458
00:39:57,730 --> 00:39:58,460
Stop!

459
00:39:59,150 --> 00:40:00,570
Stop your wailing!

460
00:40:03,580 --> 00:40:05,290
You let yourself be overcome by sorrow.

461
00:40:05,290 --> 00:40:06,460
You will drown in it.

462
00:40:06,760 --> 00:40:08,710
Have you stopped crying for your children?

463
00:40:10,260 --> 00:40:11,830
You make no sounds,

464
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:13,790
but will you ever let them go in your heart?

465
00:40:18,070 --> 00:40:19,940
They are as my flesh...

466
00:40:19,940 --> 00:40:21,470
Then who is distressed?

467
00:40:22,810 --> 00:40:25,040
Do I upset the Master and the Mistress?

468
00:40:25,190 --> 00:40:26,640
Do you care less for my loss

469
00:40:26,640 --> 00:40:27,930
than their well being?

470
00:40:27,940 --> 00:40:30,450
- Master Ford is a decent man. - He is a slaver!

471
00:40:30,450 --> 00:40:31,530
Under the circumstances...

472
00:40:31,530 --> 00:40:33,660
Under the circumstances he is a slaver!

473
00:40:33,700 --> 00:40:35,560
- But you truckle at his boot. - No.

474
00:40:35,560 --> 00:40:38,500
- You luxuriate in his favor. - I survive!

475
00:40:39,490 --> 00:40:41,430
I will not fall into despair!

476
00:40:41,490 --> 00:40:43,600
I will offer up my talents to Master Ford.

477
00:40:43,600 --> 00:40:46,440
I will keep myself hearty until freedom is opportune!

478
00:40:46,440 --> 00:40:48,430
Ford is your opportunity.

479
00:40:49,510 --> 00:40:50,520
Do you think he does not know

480
00:40:50,520 --> 00:40:52,330
that you are more than you suggest?

481
00:40:52,450 --> 00:40:55,170
But he does nothing for you. Nothing.

482
00:40:56,130 --> 00:40:58,840
You are no better than prized livestock.

483
00:40:59,970 --> 00:41:01,380
Call for him. Call,

484
00:41:01,380 --> 00:41:03,340
tell him of your previous circumstances,

485
00:41:03,340 --> 00:41:05,580
and see what it earns you, Solomon.

486
00:41:07,520 --> 00:41:09,870
So, you're settled into your role as Platt, then?

487
00:41:12,030 --> 00:41:17,430
My back is thick with scars from protesting my freedom.

488
00:41:18,190 --> 00:41:21,940
- Do not accuse me. - I accuse you of nothing.

489
00:41:22,040 --> 00:41:23,530
I cannot accuse.

490
00:41:24,270 --> 00:41:27,140
I have done dishonorable things to survive.

491
00:41:27,140 --> 00:41:29,650
And for all of them I have ended up here.

492
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:33,300
No better than if I had stood up for myself.

493
00:41:34,400 --> 00:41:35,790
God forgive me.

494
00:41:36,890 --> 00:41:39,160
Solomon, let me weep for my children.

495
00:41:50,110 --> 00:41:54,280
Whosoever therefore shall humbles himself as this little child,

496
00:41:55,050 --> 00:41:58,110
the same is greatest in the Kingdom of heaven.

497
00:41:58,930 --> 00:42:03,970
And whoso shall receive one such little child in my name

498
00:42:04,100 --> 00:42:05,900
- receiveth me. - I cannot have that kind of depression about.

499
00:42:05,900 --> 00:42:08,230
But whoso shall offend one of these little ones

500
00:42:08,230 --> 00:42:09,800
it were better for him

501
00:42:09,980 --> 00:42:12,390
that a millstone were hanged about his neck,

502
00:42:12,390 --> 00:42:15,050
and that he were drowned in the depth of the sea.

503
00:42:17,220 --> 00:42:20,250
- Amen. - Amen!

504
00:42:32,700 --> 00:42:34,400
Make them boards flush.

505
00:42:35,190 --> 00:42:35,980
They are, sir.

506
00:42:35,980 --> 00:42:37,550
No, They is no such thing.

507
00:42:39,710 --> 00:42:42,690
As smooth to the touch as a yearling's coat.

508
00:42:45,510 --> 00:42:47,520
Callin' me a liar, boy?

509
00:42:50,440 --> 00:42:52,370
Only a matter of perspective, sir.

510
00:42:53,420 --> 00:42:55,290
From where you stand you may see differently.

511
00:42:55,290 --> 00:42:56,890
But the hands are not mistaken.

512
00:42:57,130 --> 00:42:58,610
I simply ask that you

513
00:42:58,870 --> 00:43:01,320
use all your senses before rendering judgement.

514
00:43:02,850 --> 00:43:05,660
Oh... My...You are a brute.

515
00:43:07,730 --> 00:43:12,130
You are a dog, and no better for followin' instruction.

516
00:43:14,210 --> 00:43:14,970
I'll do as ordered, sir.

517
00:43:14,970 --> 00:43:16,510
Well, then you'll be up at daybreak.

518
00:43:16,510 --> 00:43:19,130
You will procure a keg of nails from Chapin;

519
00:43:19,450 --> 00:43:21,550
and commence to puttin' on clapboards.

520
00:43:21,570 --> 00:43:22,280
Yes, sir .

521
00:43:28,320 --> 00:43:29,850
Make them boards flush.

522
00:43:40,530 --> 00:43:41,190
No, please! Please, Sir!

523
00:43:41,190 --> 00:43:44,330
Where am I going, sir?

524
00:43:44,330 --> 00:43:46,840
Solomon! Solomon!

525
00:43:47,280 --> 00:43:51,120
Solomon!

526
00:43:55,020 --> 00:43:56,740
Solomon!

527
00:44:02,440 --> 00:44:04,070
When I say I had my master's favor,

528
00:44:04,070 --> 00:44:05,280
you understand.

529
00:44:08,340 --> 00:44:09,600
And for nine years

530
00:44:09,600 --> 00:44:13,400
he blessed me with every comfort and luxury in life.

531
00:44:13,700 --> 00:44:14,760
Silks and jewels

532
00:44:14,760 --> 00:44:18,300
and even servants to wait upon us.

533
00:44:20,820 --> 00:44:22,190
Such was our life,

534
00:44:23,420 --> 00:44:25,640
and the life of this beautiful girl I bore for him.

535
00:44:29,520 --> 00:44:31,040
But Master Berry's daughter...

536
00:44:32,570 --> 00:44:35,090
she always looked at me with an unkind nature.

537
00:44:36,250 --> 00:44:37,550
She hated Emily

538
00:44:37,600 --> 00:44:39,890
no matter she and Emily were flesh of flesh.

539
00:44:43,130 --> 00:44:44,530
As Master Berry's health failed,

540
00:44:44,530 --> 00:44:46,560
she gained power in the household and;

541
00:44:47,090 --> 00:44:49,630
Eventually, I was brought to the city on the false pretense

542
00:44:49,630 --> 00:44:51,950
of our free papers being executed.

543
00:44:56,480 --> 00:44:58,040
My poor children.

544
00:45:37,540 --> 00:45:40,210
I thought I told you to commence to puttin' on clapboards.

545
00:45:41,480 --> 00:45:42,580
Yes, master. I am about it.

546
00:45:42,580 --> 00:45:44,020
These have all been replaced.

547
00:45:45,620 --> 00:45:47,630
Didn't I tell yah to get a keg of nails?

548
00:45:47,980 --> 00:45:49,050
And so I did.

549
00:45:50,600 --> 00:45:51,610
So you did.

550
00:45:52,560 --> 00:45:55,700
Goddamn you! I thought you knowed somethin'!

551
00:45:55,700 --> 00:45:57,120
I did as instructed.

552
00:45:57,470 --> 00:45:58,500
If there's something wrong,

553
00:45:58,500 --> 00:46:00,320
it's wrong with your instructions.

554
00:46:00,900 --> 00:46:02,650
You, black bastard!

555
00:46:03,660 --> 00:46:04,550
You...

556
00:46:05,380 --> 00:46:06,460
goddamn...

557
00:46:07,010 --> 00:46:08,430
black bastard!

558
00:46:08,660 --> 00:46:10,280
Strip yer clothes!

559
00:46:13,030 --> 00:46:13,940
Strip!

560
00:46:15,150 --> 00:46:16,350
I will not!

561
00:46:25,830 --> 00:46:27,420
You...

562
00:46:27,420 --> 00:46:32,400
Yew will not live to see another day, nigger!

563
00:46:32,660 --> 00:46:34,240
God, help!

564
00:46:34,720 --> 00:46:35,830
Monster!

565
00:46:35,970 --> 00:46:38,040
Help! Somebody help me! Help!

566
00:46:38,140 --> 00:46:39,720
Help! Somebody!

567
00:46:50,800 --> 00:46:51,900
What is the matter?

568
00:46:52,730 --> 00:46:54,780
- What is the matter? - Master...

569
00:46:54,960 --> 00:46:56,350
Master Tibeats wants to whip me

570
00:46:56,350 --> 00:46:57,930
for using the nails you gave me.

571
00:46:59,740 --> 00:47:01,440
This ain't done by half.

572
00:47:02,250 --> 00:47:03,940
I will have flesh,

573
00:47:04,720 --> 00:47:06,620
and I will have all of it.

574
00:47:10,620 --> 00:47:11,730
Do not stir.

575
00:47:12,220 --> 00:47:13,420
Do not leave the plantation,

576
00:47:13,420 --> 00:47:15,570
for if you run I cannot protect you.

577
00:47:16,390 --> 00:47:17,180
Stay here.

578
00:48:21,070 --> 00:48:21,930
Gentlemen?

579
00:48:22,320 --> 00:48:24,600
Whoever moves that nigger is a dead man.

580
00:48:26,680 --> 00:48:29,550
I am the overseer on this plantation,

581
00:48:29,840 --> 00:48:32,640
William Ford holds a mortgage on Platt.

582
00:48:32,940 --> 00:48:35,750
If you hang him, he will lose his debt.

583
00:48:35,950 --> 00:48:38,040
You have no claim to his life.

584
00:48:38,940 --> 00:48:40,030
As for you two,

585
00:48:40,710 --> 00:48:43,230
if you have any regard for your own safety,

586
00:48:43,690 --> 00:48:44,870
I say, begone!

587
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:50,260
You got no cause.

588
00:48:50,360 --> 00:48:53,970
Platt is mine, and mine to do with as I please.

589
00:48:53,970 --> 00:48:54,970
If you touch him...

590
00:49:22,340 --> 00:49:24,740
Sam! Get the mule.

591
00:49:24,760 --> 00:49:26,000
Get Master Ford.

592
00:52:20,900 --> 00:52:22,980
Right. Right.

593
00:52:52,960 --> 00:52:55,350
I believe Tibeats is skulkin' about the premises somewhere.

594
00:52:55,350 --> 00:52:56,520
He wants you dead,

595
00:52:56,940 --> 00:52:58,160
and he will have it so.

596
00:52:58,870 --> 00:53:00,490
It's no longer safe for you here.

597
00:53:01,460 --> 00:53:04,450
And I don't believe you will remain passive if Tibeats attacks.

598
00:53:05,360 --> 00:53:08,080
I have transferred my debt to Edwin Epps.

599
00:53:08,550 --> 00:53:10,020
He will take charge of you.

600
00:53:31,070 --> 00:53:32,260
Master Ford?

601
00:53:35,010 --> 00:53:38,230
You must know that I am not a slave.

602
00:53:38,340 --> 00:53:39,430
I cannot hear that.

603
00:53:39,430 --> 00:53:41,580
Before I came to you, I was a freeman.

604
00:53:41,580 --> 00:53:43,310
I am trying to save your life!

605
00:53:45,520 --> 00:53:48,450
And... I have a debt to be mindful of.

606
00:53:50,490 --> 00:53:52,590
And that is to Edwin Epps now.

607
00:53:52,770 --> 00:53:53,660
He is a hard man.

608
00:53:53,660 --> 00:53:55,470
Prides himself on being a "Nigger breaker."

609
00:53:55,470 --> 00:53:58,190
But truthfully, I could find no others who would take you.

610
00:53:59,340 --> 00:54:01,110
You've made a reputation of yourself.

611
00:54:02,510 --> 00:54:03,770
Whatever your circumstances,

612
00:54:03,770 --> 00:54:06,840
you are an exceptional nigger, Platt.

613
00:54:09,260 --> 00:54:11,490
But I fear no good will come of it.

614
00:54:34,640 --> 00:54:35,820
"And that servant

615
00:54:37,650 --> 00:54:39,660
which knew his Lord's will...

616
00:54:41,460 --> 00:54:44,350
which knew his lord's will;

617
00:54:49,240 --> 00:54:51,180
and prepared not himself...

618
00:54:53,400 --> 00:54:55,420
prepared not himself,

619
00:55:00,030 --> 00:55:01,940
neither did according to his will,

620
00:55:04,530 --> 00:55:07,950
shall be beaten with many stripes..."

621
00:55:09,250 --> 00:55:10,170
D'ye hear that?

622
00:55:11,240 --> 00:55:12,450
"Stripes."

623
00:55:13,840 --> 00:55:15,930
That nigger that don't obey his lord,

624
00:55:15,930 --> 00:55:17,720
that's his master,d'ye see?

625
00:55:19,040 --> 00:55:23,440
that 'ere nigger shall be beaten with many stripes.

626
00:55:25,260 --> 00:55:28,250
Now, "many" signifies a great many.

627
00:55:29,640 --> 00:55:31,280
Forty, a hundred,

628
00:55:31,600 --> 00:55:33,240
a hundred and fifty lashes...

629
00:55:38,100 --> 00:55:39,350
That's Scripter!

630
00:55:56,090 --> 00:55:57,300
Pick that cotton.

631
00:55:57,840 --> 00:55:59,130
Move along now!

632
00:56:01,890 --> 00:56:02,900
Come on now!

633
00:56:04,070 --> 00:56:06,010
- Drive dem niggers. - Pick that cotton.

634
00:56:06,630 --> 00:56:07,900
Move along now,

635
00:56:08,490 --> 00:56:09,090
Hear?

636
00:56:09,090 --> 00:56:10,980
What you doing, boy? Come on!

637
00:56:13,670 --> 00:56:15,280
Two hundred forty pounds for Bob.

638
00:56:16,210 --> 00:56:17,550
What yah got for James?

639
00:56:18,580 --> 00:56:20,680
Two hundred ninety five pounds.

640
00:56:20,760 --> 00:56:23,450
Tha's real good, boy. Tha's real good.

641
00:56:24,520 --> 00:56:26,770
One hundred eighty two pounds for Platt.

642
00:56:28,340 --> 00:56:30,610
How much can even an average nigger pick a day?

643
00:56:31,280 --> 00:56:34,280
- Two hundred pounds. - This nigger ain't even average.

644
00:56:36,310 --> 00:56:38,810
Five hundred twelve pounds for Patsey.

645
00:56:42,490 --> 00:56:44,340
Yah men folk got no shame

646
00:56:44,430 --> 00:56:46,140
lettin' Patsey out pick yah?

647
00:56:48,060 --> 00:56:51,090
The day ain't yet come she swung lower than five hundred pounds.

648
00:56:54,900 --> 00:56:56,920
Queen of the fields, she is.

649
00:56:57,590 --> 00:57:00,080
- 138 pounds... - I ain't done, Treach.

650
00:57:01,150 --> 00:57:04,230
Ain't I owed a minute to luxuriate on the work Patsey done?

651
00:57:05,370 --> 00:57:06,190
Yes, sir.

652
00:57:10,650 --> 00:57:11,670
Damned Queen.

653
00:57:13,740 --> 00:57:15,860
Born and bred to the field.

654
00:57:18,360 --> 00:57:19,910
A nigger among niggers,

655
00:57:22,680 --> 00:57:24,100
and God give 'er to me.

656
00:57:28,900 --> 00:57:31,260
A lesson in the rewards of righteous livin'.

657
00:57:33,760 --> 00:57:35,500
All be observant to that.

658
00:57:37,060 --> 00:57:37,990
All!

659
00:57:39,920 --> 00:57:41,950
Now, Treach. Now speak.

660
00:57:43,250 --> 00:57:45,640
One hundred thirty eight pounds for Phebe.

661
00:57:46,840 --> 00:57:49,390
Hit one forty five yesterday. Pull her out.

662
00:57:50,700 --> 00:57:53,190
Two hundred six pounds for George.

663
00:57:53,240 --> 00:57:54,690
How much he pick yesterday?

664
00:57:56,130 --> 00:57:58,680
- Two twenty nine. - Get him out.

665
00:57:59,050 --> 00:58:00,030
Come on, kid.

666
00:58:02,470 --> 00:58:05,340
Come on. Come on, boy, move!

667
00:59:54,150 --> 00:59:56,800
Get up! We dance tonight! Get up!

668
00:59:56,800 --> 00:59:58,390
Get your fiddle, Platt! Get up!

669
00:59:58,390 --> 00:59:59,020
Come on!

670
01:00:00,610 --> 01:00:02,420
Come on, Platt! Come on!

671
01:00:14,240 --> 01:00:16,600
Come on! Where's yah merriment? Move yer feet.

672
01:00:31,350 --> 01:00:33,610
- Sell her! - What's all this?

673
01:00:33,610 --> 01:00:35,980
You will sell the negress!

674
01:00:36,380 --> 01:00:37,850
Sell little Pats?

675
01:00:38,320 --> 01:00:41,180
She pick with more vigor than any other nigger!

676
01:00:41,450 --> 01:00:43,320
- Choose another ta go. - No other.

677
01:00:44,050 --> 01:00:45,430
Sell her!

678
01:00:45,980 --> 01:00:46,940
I will not!

679
01:00:48,500 --> 01:00:51,630
You will remove that black bitch from this property,

680
01:00:51,630 --> 01:00:54,180
or I'll take myself back to Cheneyville.

681
01:00:58,490 --> 01:01:00,980
Back to that hog's trough where I found you?

682
01:01:03,730 --> 01:01:07,140
Do not set yourself up against Patsey, my dear.

683
01:01:11,510 --> 01:01:14,720
'Cause I will rid myself of yah well before I do away with her!

684
01:01:23,710 --> 01:01:24,840
Whatcha looking at?

685
01:01:26,020 --> 01:01:27,020
Damned woman!

686
01:01:28,450 --> 01:01:30,100
I won't have my mood spoiled.

687
01:01:30,930 --> 01:01:32,020
I will not.

688
01:01:34,170 --> 01:01:35,150
Dance!

689
01:01:35,860 --> 01:01:36,970
Dance, I said!

690
01:01:41,480 --> 01:01:42,210
Come on!

691
01:01:43,310 --> 01:01:45,720
Pick it up, Platt. Play that thing, boy!

692
01:02:23,050 --> 01:02:23,790
Platt?

693
01:02:26,100 --> 01:02:27,010
Yes, Mistress.

694
01:02:29,520 --> 01:02:31,690
Can you find your way to Bartholomew's?

695
01:02:32,660 --> 01:02:33,710
I can, ma'am.

696
01:02:34,370 --> 01:02:36,240
This is a list of goods and sundries.

697
01:02:36,240 --> 01:02:38,830
You will take it to be filled and return immediately.

698
01:02:39,680 --> 01:02:40,970
Take your tag.

699
01:02:41,660 --> 01:02:44,720
- Tell Bartholomew to add it to our debt. - Yes, Mistress.

700
01:02:46,840 --> 01:02:48,480
Where yah from, Platt?

701
01:02:51,060 --> 01:02:53,540
- I have told you. - Tell me again.

702
01:02:54,830 --> 01:02:56,920
- Washington. - Who were yah Master?

703
01:02:56,920 --> 01:02:59,500
- Master's name was Freeman. - Was he a learned man?

704
01:03:00,880 --> 01:03:04,040
- I suppose so. - He learn yah ta read?

705
01:03:05,940 --> 01:03:07,680
A word here or there,

706
01:03:08,690 --> 01:03:10,250
but I have no understanding of the written text.

707
01:03:10,250 --> 01:03:12,010
Don't trouble yer self with it.

708
01:03:12,820 --> 01:03:14,990
Same as the rest, Master bought yah to work.

709
01:03:14,990 --> 01:03:15,950
Tha's all.

710
01:03:17,620 --> 01:03:19,810
And any more'll earn yah a hundred lashes.

711
01:04:26,290 --> 01:04:27,270
Come here, boy.

712
01:04:30,190 --> 01:04:31,140
Come on.

713
01:04:47,720 --> 01:04:50,470
- Where are you going, boy? - On my way to

714
01:04:50,750 --> 01:04:54,090
Bartholomew's... sent by Mistress Epps.

715
01:04:58,290 --> 01:04:59,660
You best get there then.

716
01:05:01,320 --> 01:05:02,400
Get there quick.

717
01:05:51,870 --> 01:05:54,300
- Any trouble? - No, ma'am.

718
01:05:54,830 --> 01:05:55,700
No trouble.

719
01:06:54,650 --> 01:06:56,420
Platt Epps, good Sunday morning.

720
01:06:56,420 --> 01:06:57,700
Good morning, Master Shaw.

721
01:06:57,840 --> 01:07:00,450
Master sent me to retrieve Patsey. May I approach?

722
01:07:00,450 --> 01:07:01,340
You may.

723
01:07:12,360 --> 01:07:13,680
Excuse me, Mistress Shaw.

724
01:07:14,370 --> 01:07:17,650
- Nigger Platt. - Patsey, Master wishes you to return.

725
01:07:17,730 --> 01:07:19,710
The Sabbath day. I's free ta roam.

726
01:07:19,880 --> 01:07:21,060
Master sent me running to fetch you,

727
01:07:21,070 --> 01:07:22,830
and said no time should be wasted.

728
01:07:22,830 --> 01:07:26,250
- Drink a tea? - Thank you, Mistress, but I don't dare.

729
01:07:26,610 --> 01:07:28,680
Would you know Massa Epps's consternation

730
01:07:28,680 --> 01:07:31,270
to be any lessened wit your timely return?

731
01:07:32,660 --> 01:07:34,820
Ain't it his constant condition?

732
01:07:35,080 --> 01:07:38,220
Sit. Sit and drink the tea that offered.

733
01:07:43,890 --> 01:07:45,700
What'n be Epps's concern?

734
01:07:47,820 --> 01:07:49,230
I'd rather not say.

735
01:07:50,180 --> 01:07:52,620
L'il gossip on the Sabbath be fine.

736
01:07:52,660 --> 01:07:54,610
All things in moderation.

737
01:07:56,040 --> 01:07:59,290
As you are aware, Master Epps...

738
01:07:59,790 --> 01:08:03,490
is a man of hard countenance.

739
01:08:04,540 --> 01:08:06,860
You know he has ill feeling toward your husband.

740
01:08:06,870 --> 01:08:07,740
He do.

741
01:08:08,980 --> 01:08:10,510
Master Epps has somehow come to believe,

742
01:08:10,510 --> 01:08:12,170
that Master Shaw...

743
01:08:13,690 --> 01:08:15,410
is something of a lothario.

744
01:08:16,850 --> 01:08:19,030
A misguided belief, no doubt.

745
01:08:19,450 --> 01:08:23,000
No doubt... if not born outta truth itself.

746
01:08:25,220 --> 01:08:26,720
I meant no disrespect.

747
01:08:27,180 --> 01:08:28,720
He ain't heard you.

748
01:08:29,360 --> 01:08:31,600
I meant no disrespect to you, Mistress.

749
01:08:34,640 --> 01:08:37,710
Got no cause to worry for my sensibilities.

750
01:08:38,840 --> 01:08:43,060
I ain't felt the end of a lash in 'mo years than I cain recall.

751
01:08:43,550 --> 01:08:45,450
I ain't worked a field, neither.

752
01:08:46,360 --> 01:08:50,680
Where once I served, now I have others servin' me.

753
01:08:51,970 --> 01:08:55,860
The cost to my current existence be Massa Shaw..

754
01:08:55,950 --> 01:08:57,880
broadcasting his affections and

755
01:08:57,990 --> 01:09:00,960
me enjoyin' the pantomime of his fidelity.

756
01:09:02,210 --> 01:09:04,620
If that what keep me from the cotton pickin' niggers,

757
01:09:04,810 --> 01:09:06,000
that what it be.

758
01:09:06,910 --> 01:09:10,100
A small and reasonable price to be paid 'fo sure.

759
01:09:14,820 --> 01:09:15,930
I knowed what it like

760
01:09:15,940 --> 01:09:20,460
to be the object of Massa's predilections and peculiarities.

761
01:09:21,340 --> 01:09:23,330
A lusty visit in the night,

762
01:09:24,150 --> 01:09:26,260
or a visitation with the whip.

763
01:09:27,990 --> 01:09:29,500
Take comfort, Patsey;

764
01:09:29,760 --> 01:09:31,540
Good Lord will manage Epps.

765
01:09:32,340 --> 01:09:36,220
In His own time the Good Lord will manage dem all.

766
01:09:37,230 --> 01:09:38,880
The curse of the pharaohs

767
01:09:38,910 --> 01:09:43,060
were a poor example of all that wait 'fo the plantation class.

768
01:09:49,010 --> 01:09:50,140
This is nice.

769
01:10:01,900 --> 01:10:02,800
Patsey?

770
01:10:04,280 --> 01:10:06,560
- Patsey! - Do not look in his direction. Continue on.

771
01:10:06,900 --> 01:10:08,480
- Patsey! - Found her, Master,

772
01:10:09,260 --> 01:10:11,000
and brought her back just as instructed.

773
01:10:14,160 --> 01:10:15,580
What'd you jus now tell her?

774
01:10:16,520 --> 01:10:17,750
What'd you say to Pats?

775
01:10:19,230 --> 01:10:21,320
No words were spoken. None of consequence.

776
01:10:22,900 --> 01:10:25,860
Lie! Damned liar!

777
01:10:27,460 --> 01:10:28,670
Saw you talkin' with 'er.

778
01:10:30,640 --> 01:10:31,500
Tell me!

779
01:10:33,810 --> 01:10:35,370
I cannot speak of what did not occur.

780
01:10:35,780 --> 01:10:38,270
- I'll cut your black throat. - Master...

781
01:10:39,510 --> 01:10:40,400
You come here!

782
01:10:41,150 --> 01:10:42,550
- Master, I brought... - I said come here!

783
01:10:42,550 --> 01:10:43,780
I brought her back, just like you ...

784
01:10:45,380 --> 01:10:47,970
- Come here! - Come on, let's go!

785
01:10:52,560 --> 01:10:54,200
I got her, just as instructed.

786
01:10:57,650 --> 01:10:59,040
Stay away from Pats, boy!

787
01:11:33,420 --> 01:11:34,530
It's the Lord's day.

788
01:11:36,870 --> 01:11:39,330
Ain't nothin' Christian in us carryin' on like this.

789
01:11:46,570 --> 01:11:47,850
I concede to yah,

790
01:11:50,890 --> 01:11:52,060
but in the name of valor,

791
01:11:53,640 --> 01:11:55,240
help yer master to his feet.

792
01:12:01,190 --> 01:12:02,420
What's the fuss?

793
01:12:02,860 --> 01:12:04,960
Master Epps believed Patsey and me to be in conversation

794
01:12:04,960 --> 01:12:05,990
when we were not.

795
01:12:06,490 --> 01:12:08,130
I tried to explain, but it's led to all this.

796
01:12:08,130 --> 01:12:09,100
What is it?

797
01:12:09,190 --> 01:12:11,810
Ya can't remain the Sabbath without her under your eye?

798
01:12:11,810 --> 01:12:14,070
- Hold on... - Ya are a no-account bastard.

799
01:12:14,100 --> 01:12:16,160
A filthy, godless heathen.

800
01:12:16,160 --> 01:12:18,220
My bed is too holy for yah ta share.

801
01:12:18,970 --> 01:12:21,440
- Wha's he been tellin' yah? - Of yer misbegotten ways.

802
01:12:21,440 --> 01:12:23,270
And he would know what of anythin'?

803
01:12:24,870 --> 01:12:26,600
I ain't even spoken with him today.

804
01:12:27,550 --> 01:12:29,030
Yah lyin' nigger, Platt.

805
01:12:30,020 --> 01:12:30,880
Have I?

806
01:12:33,530 --> 01:12:34,380
Have I?

807
01:12:37,180 --> 01:12:39,340
There. There's all the truth he got.

808
01:12:40,780 --> 01:12:41,750
Damned nigger.

809
01:14:33,890 --> 01:14:34,840
Patsey?

810
01:16:31,910 --> 01:16:34,330
A moment from the dancing.

811
01:16:35,620 --> 01:16:37,890
Come sample what I baked for y'all.

812
01:16:37,890 --> 01:16:39,650
- Thank you, Mistress! - Thank you, Mistress!

813
01:16:39,650 --> 01:16:41,300
- Thank you, Mistress! - Thank you, Mistress!

814
01:16:41,300 --> 01:16:43,940
- Thank you, Mistress. - There'll be none for you, Patsey.

815
01:16:45,570 --> 01:16:46,970
Yah see that?

816
01:16:47,500 --> 01:16:50,180
Yah see that look of insolence she give me?

817
01:16:51,160 --> 01:16:52,740
Seen nothin' but her turn away.

818
01:16:52,740 --> 01:16:55,120
Are you blind or ignorant?

819
01:16:55,130 --> 01:16:57,500
It was hot, hateful scorn.

820
01:16:57,500 --> 01:16:59,700
It filled that black face.

821
01:17:00,170 --> 01:17:03,630
Yah tell me yah did'n see it, then yah choose not to look,

822
01:17:03,630 --> 01:17:05,480
or yah sayin' I lie.

823
01:17:05,700 --> 01:17:07,820
Whatever it was, it passed.

824
01:17:08,670 --> 01:17:11,450
Is that how yah are with the niggers?

825
01:17:12,040 --> 01:17:15,250
Lettin' every ill thought fester inside 'em.

826
01:17:16,040 --> 01:17:17,250
Look at them.

827
01:17:17,590 --> 01:17:19,370
They foul with it;

828
01:17:19,880 --> 01:17:22,220
They foul with their hate.

829
01:17:22,650 --> 01:17:26,230
You let it be, it's gonna come back to us in the dark a night.

830
01:17:26,910 --> 01:17:28,200
Yah want that?

831
01:17:29,150 --> 01:17:30,890
Yah want them black animals

832
01:17:30,890 --> 01:17:33,790
leave us gut like pigs in our own sleep?

833
01:17:35,150 --> 01:17:36,310
No...

834
01:17:36,880 --> 01:17:39,780
You are manless.

835
01:17:40,220 --> 01:17:42,620
A damned eunuch if ever there was.

836
01:17:43,510 --> 01:17:44,930
And if yah won't stand for me,

837
01:17:44,930 --> 01:17:47,480
I'd pray you'd at least be a credit to yer own kind,

838
01:17:47,480 --> 01:17:49,860
and beat every foul thought from 'em.

839
01:18:00,110 --> 01:18:01,480
Beat it from 'em!

840
01:18:18,410 --> 01:18:19,790
Eat!

841
01:18:20,350 --> 01:18:22,050
Fill yourselves.

842
01:18:22,850 --> 01:18:24,360
And then we dance.

843
01:18:29,350 --> 01:18:30,750
I said, eat!

844
01:18:46,930 --> 01:18:47,910
Platt...

845
01:18:49,740 --> 01:18:51,260
Platt, you awake?

846
01:18:54,760 --> 01:18:55,790
I am.

847
01:18:57,130 --> 01:18:59,130
I have a request.

848
01:18:59,840 --> 01:19:01,580
An act of kindness.

849
01:19:05,280 --> 01:19:07,560
I secreted it from the Mistress.

850
01:19:09,650 --> 01:19:11,940
- Return it! - It yours, Platt.

851
01:19:13,590 --> 01:19:14,960
For what cause?

852
01:19:15,330 --> 01:19:19,540
All I ask is end my life.

853
01:19:20,790 --> 01:19:23,890
Take my body to the margin of the swamp.

854
01:19:24,130 --> 01:19:27,250
Take me by the throat. Hold me low in the water

855
01:19:27,250 --> 01:19:29,880
until I's still 'n without life.

856
01:19:30,550 --> 01:19:32,380
Bury me in a lonely place of dyin'.

857
01:19:32,380 --> 01:19:34,140
I will do no such thing.

858
01:19:35,430 --> 01:19:37,270
The gory detail with which you speak...

859
01:19:37,270 --> 01:19:39,740
I thought on it long and hard.

860
01:19:41,250 --> 01:19:42,900
It is melancholia,

861
01:19:43,850 --> 01:19:45,140
nothing more.

862
01:19:46,510 --> 01:19:49,000
How can you fall into such despair?

863
01:19:49,510 --> 01:19:52,090
How can you not know?

864
01:19:54,330 --> 01:19:58,350
I ain't got no comfort in this life.

865
01:20:00,920 --> 01:20:06,870
If I cain't buy mercy from yah, I'll beg it.

866
01:20:07,480 --> 01:20:08,660
There are others.

867
01:20:10,010 --> 01:20:10,510
Beg them.

868
01:20:10,510 --> 01:20:12,480
- I'm begging you! - Why?

869
01:20:13,410 --> 01:20:14,620
Why would you consign me

870
01:20:14,620 --> 01:20:17,370
to damnation with such an un-Godly request?

871
01:20:17,380 --> 01:20:19,370
There is God here!

872
01:20:20,220 --> 01:20:23,430
God is merciful,

873
01:20:23,870 --> 01:20:26,880
and He forgive merciful acts.

874
01:20:26,890 --> 01:20:29,150
Won't be no hell for you.

875
01:20:31,440 --> 01:20:32,570
Do it.

876
01:20:37,800 --> 01:20:41,270
Do what I ain't got the strength ta do myself.

877
01:21:20,270 --> 01:21:21,720
It is a plague.

878
01:21:23,030 --> 01:21:27,160
- It's cotton worm. - It's a plague! It's damn Biblical.

879
01:21:28,250 --> 01:21:31,390
Two seasons God don't sent a plague to smite me.

880
01:21:33,550 --> 01:21:35,840
What I done that God hate me so?

881
01:21:43,190 --> 01:21:44,900
It's that Godless lot.

882
01:21:47,290 --> 01:21:48,900
They brought this on me.

883
01:21:49,230 --> 01:21:51,250
I bring 'em God's word, and heathens they are,

884
01:21:51,250 --> 01:21:53,200
they brought me God's scorn.

885
01:21:57,660 --> 01:21:58,680
Damn you!

886
01:21:59,450 --> 01:22:00,530
Damn you!

887
01:22:01,870 --> 01:22:03,330
Damn all, you all!

888
01:22:31,120 --> 01:22:33,800
- Judge? - Mr. Epps.

889
01:22:35,560 --> 01:22:39,080
I am deeply sadden to hear about your misfortune.

890
01:22:40,280 --> 01:22:42,320
?

891
01:22:44,340 --> 01:22:45,500
Listen up.

892
01:22:45,940 --> 01:22:47,350
Yer Judge Turner's for the season.

893
01:22:47,350 --> 01:22:48,190
More if need be,

894
01:22:48,200 --> 01:22:49,740
until my crop return.

895
01:22:50,480 --> 01:22:52,580
Yah'll bring no disrespect to me,

896
01:22:53,030 --> 01:22:55,420
and yah'll bring no biblical plagues to him. You hear?

897
01:22:56,070 --> 01:22:57,710
Or I'll take all your skin.

898
01:22:59,050 --> 01:22:59,960
Get out.

899
01:23:52,590 --> 01:23:54,450
Get off the porch! You ain't supposed to be on the porch.

900
01:23:54,450 --> 01:23:55,720
Get off the porch!

901
01:24:02,580 --> 01:24:03,720
Platt is it?

902
01:24:04,470 --> 01:24:07,860
- Yes , sir. - Have you cultivated cane previously?

903
01:24:09,120 --> 01:24:12,320
- No, sir. I am not. - It comes to you quite naturally.

904
01:24:12,900 --> 01:24:14,800
- Are you educated? - No, sir.

905
01:24:14,800 --> 01:24:17,090
Niggers are hired to work, not read or write.

906
01:24:19,790 --> 01:24:22,680
- You play the fiddle? - Yes , sir.

907
01:24:22,680 --> 01:24:23,700
Yes, I do.

908
01:24:24,900 --> 01:24:27,210
Willard Yarney, a planter up the bayou,

909
01:24:27,210 --> 01:24:30,290
celebrates his anniversary in a three week's time.

910
01:24:30,750 --> 01:24:32,810
I will hold out your name to him.

911
01:24:33,210 --> 01:24:35,450
What you earn is yours to keep.

912
01:24:36,350 --> 01:24:37,340
Yes, sir.

913
01:24:38,110 --> 01:24:39,620
Mind yourself, Platt.

914
01:27:03,930 --> 01:27:05,640
Joyous day.

915
01:27:06,020 --> 01:27:07,800
Joyous day.

916
01:27:08,680 --> 01:27:10,910
Dark times is behind us.

917
01:27:11,100 --> 01:27:14,560
Clean livin' 'n prayer done lifted the plague.

918
01:27:16,430 --> 01:27:19,840
As thick 'n white as New England snow.

919
01:27:21,770 --> 01:27:23,970
'N now my niggers is returned to me.

920
01:27:28,370 --> 01:27:30,520
Heard Judge Turner gave you favor.

921
01:27:35,080 --> 01:27:36,750
Oh, did you beguile him, Platt,

922
01:27:37,360 --> 01:27:39,310
with your slick nigger ways?

923
01:27:42,950 --> 01:27:44,760
Well, yah won't stand idle, boy.

924
01:27:45,530 --> 01:27:46,910
Not on my land.

925
01:27:50,220 --> 01:27:51,630
Much work to do.

926
01:27:54,160 --> 01:27:57,270
Days of old long since, eh?

927
01:28:04,070 --> 01:28:08,630
Joyous! Joyous indeed!

928
01:28:10,790 --> 01:28:13,680
Let's go find something sweet for you. Hmm?

929
01:28:16,010 --> 01:28:17,710
- Candy. - Candy?

930
01:28:45,660 --> 01:28:48,580
- George? - One hundred and eighty pounds.

931
01:28:48,930 --> 01:28:53,120
- Patsey? - Five hundred twenty pounds for Patsey.

932
01:28:53,120 --> 01:28:55,720
Tha's my girl. Don't never let me down.

933
01:28:56,180 --> 01:29:00,020
- Platt? - One hundred sixty pounds.

934
01:29:01,600 --> 01:29:02,820
Armsby?

935
01:29:03,690 --> 01:29:05,340
Sixty four pounds.

936
01:29:10,470 --> 01:29:12,740
A good days labor would average two hundred pounds.

937
01:29:12,740 --> 01:29:13,660
Yes, sir.

938
01:29:18,640 --> 01:29:21,040
I'm sure in time y'll develope as a picker,

939
01:29:21,780 --> 01:29:23,480
but it takes effort, boy.

940
01:29:25,320 --> 01:29:28,360
- Put some damn effort into it. - Yes, sir.

941
01:29:28,370 --> 01:29:30,270
Take 'em out. Get to whippin'.

942
01:29:37,090 --> 01:29:38,570
It's a tragedy.

943
01:29:40,150 --> 01:29:42,140
How does such come to pass?

944
01:29:42,920 --> 01:29:45,990
Working a field and picking cotton like a lowly hand.

945
01:29:46,650 --> 01:29:48,930
I'm of a damn sight better station.

946
01:29:50,090 --> 01:29:52,100
I've worked as an overseer, you know.

947
01:29:52,420 --> 01:29:55,140
- I did not know, sir. - Not "Sir."

948
01:29:56,110 --> 01:29:57,450
Just Armsby.

949
01:29:58,800 --> 01:30:01,090
Not owed more than any other in the field.

950
01:30:01,090 --> 01:30:04,020
How did you arrive at such a place, if I may ask?

951
01:30:04,560 --> 01:30:06,620
Ask. It's just conversation.

952
01:30:09,210 --> 01:30:11,860
I became a little too dependant on the whisky,

953
01:30:12,380 --> 01:30:14,530
a little too undependable on the job.

954
01:30:16,140 --> 01:30:19,050
Before you say I'm just a sorry drunkard,

955
01:30:19,050 --> 01:30:20,680
let me state my case:

956
01:30:22,200 --> 01:30:24,220
As reliable employment as overseeing is,

957
01:30:24,220 --> 01:30:26,580
it's no easy chore on the spirit.

958
01:30:27,350 --> 01:30:30,180
I say no man of conscious;

959
01:30:30,340 --> 01:30:32,970
can take the lash to another human day in and day out

960
01:30:32,970 --> 01:30:34,980
without shredding at his own self.

961
01:30:36,300 --> 01:30:38,140
Takes him to a place...

962
01:30:38,630 --> 01:30:42,520
where he either makes excuses within his mind to be unaffected...

963
01:30:43,680 --> 01:30:46,400
or finds some way to trample his guilty sensations.

964
01:30:46,400 --> 01:30:49,260
Well, I trampled,

965
01:30:49,750 --> 01:30:51,150
with frequency.

966
01:30:53,130 --> 01:30:56,230
I gave in to tales of wealth and prosperity,

967
01:30:56,720 --> 01:31:00,840
but such profitable outcomes

968
01:31:00,840 --> 01:31:03,500
are reserved for the plantation masters.

969
01:31:04,540 --> 01:31:07,210
It's the lot of the rest of us to serve.

970
01:31:09,420 --> 01:31:12,540
Now, all I want is to earn a decent wage

971
01:31:12,540 --> 01:31:14,240
and get myself home.

972
01:31:47,000 --> 01:31:49,330
The proceeds of my fiddling performances.

973
01:31:49,940 --> 01:31:51,720
Just a few picayunes,

974
01:31:52,160 --> 01:31:54,080
but all I have in the world.

975
01:31:54,580 --> 01:31:58,150
I promise them to you if you will do me the favor I require.

976
01:31:58,150 --> 01:32:01,790
But I beg you not to expose me if you cannot grant the request.

977
01:32:04,440 --> 01:32:05,270
What...

978
01:32:05,270 --> 01:32:08,030
- What is it that you ask? - First, your word, sir.

979
01:32:09,370 --> 01:32:10,660
On my honor.

980
01:32:12,390 --> 01:32:14,320
It is a simple enough request.

981
01:32:15,840 --> 01:32:18,000
I only ask you to post a letter

982
01:32:18,170 --> 01:32:19,660
at the post office in Marksville

983
01:32:19,660 --> 01:32:22,810
and that you keep the action an inviolable secret forever.

984
01:32:26,450 --> 01:32:29,080
A patron is what I require, sir.

985
01:32:35,440 --> 01:32:36,460
I'll do it.

986
01:32:37,260 --> 01:32:39,510
And I will accept whatever payment is offered.

987
01:32:42,500 --> 01:32:44,940
To assist you, I put my own self at risk.

988
01:32:45,840 --> 01:32:47,140
I will do so,

989
01:32:47,810 --> 01:32:50,330
but fair compensation is all I ask.

990
01:33:00,460 --> 01:33:01,770
Draw up your letter.

991
01:33:02,570 --> 01:33:04,840
We will meet again. In two days?

992
01:33:06,710 --> 01:33:07,980
In two days.

993
01:33:11,270 --> 01:33:12,270
Thank you.

994
01:34:30,440 --> 01:34:31,810
Well, boy.

995
01:34:32,440 --> 01:34:35,080
I understand I've got a learned nigger

996
01:34:35,550 --> 01:34:37,230
that writes letters...

997
01:34:38,320 --> 01:34:40,750
and tries to get white fellows to mail 'em.

998
01:34:47,700 --> 01:34:49,850
Well, Armsby tol' me today

999
01:34:50,500 --> 01:34:52,780
the devil was among my niggers.

1000
01:34:54,730 --> 01:34:57,060
that I have one that needed watchin'

1001
01:34:57,900 --> 01:34:59,390
or he would run away.

1002
01:35:02,140 --> 01:35:03,780
When I asked him why

1003
01:35:04,980 --> 01:35:08,170
he said you come over to him,

1004
01:35:08,630 --> 01:35:10,910
and waked him up in the middle of the night,

1005
01:35:11,650 --> 01:35:13,960
and wanted him to carry a letter

1006
01:35:15,460 --> 01:35:16,760
to Marksville.

1007
01:35:22,330 --> 01:35:23,930
What yah got to say to that?

1008
01:35:27,460 --> 01:35:28,950
There is no truth to it.

1009
01:35:30,260 --> 01:35:31,470
You say.

1010
01:35:33,400 --> 01:35:35,770
How could I write a letter without ink or paper?

1011
01:35:37,420 --> 01:35:38,140
Who am I going to write to?

1012
01:35:38,140 --> 01:35:40,330
I got no friends living as I know of.

1013
01:35:42,050 --> 01:35:43,280
That Armsby...

1014
01:35:45,090 --> 01:35:48,430
That Armsby is a lying drunken fellow.

1015
01:35:50,500 --> 01:35:52,770
Didn't he want you to hire him as an overseer?

1016
01:35:55,290 --> 01:35:56,340
That's it.

1017
01:35:58,270 --> 01:36:00,400
He wants to make you believe we're all going to run away

1018
01:36:00,400 --> 01:36:02,590
so you'll hire him an overseer.

1019
01:36:04,330 --> 01:36:06,070
He believes you are soft soap,

1020
01:36:07,750 --> 01:36:09,490
and he's given to such talk,

1021
01:36:10,960 --> 01:36:14,600
made this story out of whole cloth,

1022
01:36:15,290 --> 01:36:17,190
because he wants the situation.

1023
01:36:23,020 --> 01:36:25,190
It's all a lie, master.

1024
01:36:30,990 --> 01:36:32,420
It's all a lie.

1025
01:36:41,130 --> 01:36:42,640
I'll be damned.

1026
01:36:49,190 --> 01:36:51,490
Were he not free and white, Platt.

1027
01:36:53,990 --> 01:36:56,000
Were he not free and white.

1028
01:38:27,730 --> 01:38:30,460
Edward? Give him water!

1029
01:38:38,360 --> 01:38:39,260
Get up.

1030
01:38:40,670 --> 01:38:41,540
Get up.

1031
01:38:48,610 --> 01:38:49,790
Nigger, get up.

1032
01:38:56,040 --> 01:38:57,270
What are you looking at, boy?

1033
01:38:59,690 --> 01:39:00,910
Keep picking, boy.

1034
01:39:14,690 --> 01:39:16,240
I just want to say something

1035
01:39:16,840 --> 01:39:18,000
'bout Uncle Abram.

1036
01:39:22,560 --> 01:39:23,700
He was a good man

1037
01:39:25,050 --> 01:39:27,530
and he always looked out for us, ever since we were little.

1038
01:39:29,030 --> 01:39:30,040
God love him.

1039
01:39:31,330 --> 01:39:33,690
God bless him. God keep him.

1040
01:39:34,980 --> 01:39:35,820
Amen.

1041
01:42:02,510 --> 01:42:03,800
Wait till the end.

1042
01:42:12,550 --> 01:42:13,670
Hey, Bass?

1043
01:42:14,990 --> 01:42:16,430
No, no, no...

1044
01:42:16,700 --> 01:42:19,000
No shame in taking respite from the heat,

1045
01:42:19,410 --> 01:42:20,670
drink, shade.

1046
01:42:21,230 --> 01:42:24,410
It's ungodly for travelers. Hearty, or otherwise.

1047
01:42:28,900 --> 01:42:32,410
- What's funny ? - Epps, I'm here to finish the work at hand.

1048
01:42:32,420 --> 01:42:35,460
As requested and as paid for.

1049
01:42:35,740 --> 01:42:37,630
Something rubs you wrongly.

1050
01:42:37,930 --> 01:42:40,220
I offer you the opportunity to speak off.

1051
01:42:43,990 --> 01:42:47,060
Well. You ask plainly, so I will tell you plainly.

1052
01:42:47,510 --> 01:42:49,360
What amused me just then, was...

1053
01:42:49,440 --> 01:42:52,020
your concern for my well being in this heat,

1054
01:42:52,020 --> 01:42:53,370
when quite frankly,

1055
01:42:53,370 --> 01:42:55,180
the conditions of your labours...

1056
01:42:55,200 --> 01:42:56,980
- The condition of my labour? - It is hard!

1057
01:42:56,980 --> 01:43:00,000
- What the hell? - It's all wrong. All wrong, Mr. Epps.

1058
01:43:00,000 --> 01:43:01,630
They ain't hired to help.

1059
01:43:02,330 --> 01:43:03,670
They are my property.

1060
01:43:04,290 --> 01:43:06,760
- You say that with pride. - I say it as fact.

1061
01:43:09,240 --> 01:43:12,700
This conversation concerns what is fact and what's not.

1062
01:43:13,040 --> 01:43:14,790
Then it must be said.

1063
01:43:14,790 --> 01:43:18,280
That there is no justice, or righteousness in this slavery.

1064
01:43:18,880 --> 01:43:21,200
But you do open up a interesting question.

1065
01:43:22,030 --> 01:43:23,970
What right have you to your niggers

1066
01:43:23,970 --> 01:43:26,560
- when you come down to the point? - What right?

1067
01:43:27,400 --> 01:43:30,190
I bought them, I paid for them.

1068
01:43:30,770 --> 01:43:31,370
Of course you did,

1069
01:43:31,370 --> 01:43:34,100
and the law say's you have the right to hold a nigger.

1070
01:43:34,420 --> 01:43:36,810
But begging the laws pardon, it lies.

1071
01:43:36,890 --> 01:43:39,680
Suppose they pass the law, take away your liberty,

1072
01:43:39,820 --> 01:43:41,220
making you a slave.

1073
01:43:41,410 --> 01:43:44,470
- Suppose. - That ain't a supposable case.

1074
01:43:44,470 --> 01:43:48,200
Laws change, Epps. Universal truths though are constant.

1075
01:43:48,200 --> 01:43:51,300
It is a fact, a plain and simple fact

1076
01:43:51,300 --> 01:43:54,160
that what is true and right is true and right for all.

1077
01:43:54,680 --> 01:43:56,390
White and black alike.

1078
01:43:58,290 --> 01:44:00,260
Yah compare me to a nigger, Bass?

1079
01:44:00,390 --> 01:44:03,890
I am only asking, in the eye's of God, what is the difference?

1080
01:44:05,170 --> 01:44:05,800
Yah might as well ask

1081
01:44:05,800 --> 01:44:09,230
what the difference is between a white man and a baboon.

1082
01:44:10,500 --> 01:44:13,350
Now, I've seen one of them critters in Orleans

1083
01:44:13,460 --> 01:44:15,670
that knowed just as much as any nigger I got.

1084
01:44:16,210 --> 01:44:19,740
Listen, Epps... These niggers are human beings.

1085
01:44:19,740 --> 01:44:22,300
If they are allowed to claim no higher than brute animals,

1086
01:44:22,300 --> 01:44:25,030
you and men like you will have to answer for it.

1087
01:44:25,860 --> 01:44:27,960
There's an ill, Mr. Epps,

1088
01:44:28,280 --> 01:44:31,100
a fearful ill, resting upon this nation,

1089
01:44:31,430 --> 01:44:33,840
and there will be a day of reckoning yet.

1090
01:44:36,940 --> 01:44:39,260
You like to hear yourself talk, Bass,

1091
01:44:39,780 --> 01:44:41,740
better than any man I know of.

1092
01:44:42,980 --> 01:44:46,540
Yah argue that black was white, or white black.

1093
01:44:46,770 --> 01:44:48,550
If anybody contradict you,

1094
01:44:50,990 --> 01:44:54,300
a fine supposition if yah lived among Yankees in New England.

1095
01:44:54,560 --> 01:44:55,720
But yah don't.

1096
01:44:59,710 --> 01:45:01,460
You most assuredly do not.

1097
01:45:27,470 --> 01:45:29,520
I know it's somewhere in there!

1098
01:45:32,260 --> 01:45:33,340
Patsey!

1099
01:45:35,620 --> 01:45:36,710
Pats!

1100
01:45:37,710 --> 01:45:38,760
Where is she?

1101
01:45:39,860 --> 01:45:41,110
Where is Pats?

1102
01:45:41,380 --> 01:45:43,380
Where is she? Tell me, where is she?

1103
01:45:46,940 --> 01:45:48,640
Where is she? Where is Pats? Where is she?

1104
01:45:48,640 --> 01:45:50,280
Whatcha standing there for?

1105
01:45:50,280 --> 01:45:52,280
- We know nothin' of her, massa. - Know none of what?

1106
01:45:52,280 --> 01:45:53,980
- We know nothin' of her. - Of what?

1107
01:45:53,980 --> 01:45:55,550
- Where did she go? - I do not know.

1108
01:45:55,550 --> 01:45:56,850
- She run off, ain't she? - I know nothing.

1109
01:45:56,850 --> 01:45:58,860
She ran off! Where is she?

1110
01:45:58,990 --> 01:45:59,570
?

1111
01:45:59,570 --> 01:46:03,630
- You know! You know! You know! - No, no, no...

1112
01:46:03,630 --> 01:46:05,290
No I don't.

1113
01:46:07,620 --> 01:46:11,870
You miserable black dogs stand like the deef and dumb.

1114
01:46:14,040 --> 01:46:15,190
Speak!

1115
01:46:30,540 --> 01:46:31,710
She's gone...

1116
01:46:34,540 --> 01:46:36,210
My Pats is gone.

1117
01:46:53,520 --> 01:46:55,620
Run off. Run off, did you?

1118
01:46:55,620 --> 01:46:57,710
- Massa Epps... - You miserable wench! Where have you been?

1119
01:46:57,710 --> 01:47:00,470
- I've been nowhere. - Lies to your misdeeds!

1120
01:47:00,470 --> 01:47:03,280
The Sabbath day, massa. I took me a walk to commune with the Lord.

1121
01:47:03,290 --> 01:47:04,760
Bring the Lord into yer deceptions?

1122
01:47:04,770 --> 01:47:06,780
Yah comin' from Shaw's plantation, weren't yah?

1123
01:47:06,780 --> 01:47:09,130
- No. - Now yah speak?

1124
01:47:09,130 --> 01:47:11,310
Now that yah want to add to her lies yah find yer tongue!

1125
01:47:11,320 --> 01:47:13,450
I went to Massa Shaw's plantation!

1126
01:47:14,240 --> 01:47:15,830
- You admit it? - Yes.

1127
01:47:16,050 --> 01:47:18,550
Freely. And you know why?

1128
01:47:19,120 --> 01:47:21,560
I got this from Mistress Shaw.

1129
01:47:22,140 --> 01:47:26,210
Mistress Epps won't even grant me no soap ta clean with.

1130
01:47:26,700 --> 01:47:30,390
I stink so much I make myself gag.

1131
01:47:33,570 --> 01:47:39,020
Five hundred pounds of cotton day in, day out!

1132
01:47:39,110 --> 01:47:40,790
More than any man here.

1133
01:47:41,120 --> 01:47:43,150
And for that I will be clean;

1134
01:47:43,410 --> 01:47:45,010
that's all I ask.

1135
01:47:45,200 --> 01:47:48,120
Dis here what I went to Shaw's 'fo.

1136
01:47:49,790 --> 01:47:54,610
- Liar! - Lord knows it all!

1137
01:47:54,780 --> 01:47:59,170
- You Liar! - And you blind wit yer own covetousness.

1138
01:48:00,130 --> 01:48:02,140
I don't lie, Massa.

1139
01:48:02,720 --> 01:48:05,780
If you kill me, I'll stick to that.

1140
01:48:06,710 --> 01:48:08,070
Yeah, I'll set you down.

1141
01:48:09,150 --> 01:48:10,840
I'll learn you to go to Shaw's.

1142
01:48:11,590 --> 01:48:12,550
Treach!

1143
01:48:14,800 --> 01:48:16,180
Go fetch some line.

1144
01:48:16,460 --> 01:48:17,310
Edward?

1145
01:48:19,150 --> 01:48:21,980
Strip her. Strike her bare 'n lash her to the post.

1146
01:48:25,730 --> 01:48:26,690
No!

1147
01:48:40,720 --> 01:48:42,600
Yah done this to yourself, Pats!

1148
01:48:54,590 --> 01:48:55,460
Do it!

1149
01:49:00,810 --> 01:49:02,700
Strike the life from her.

1150
01:49:09,120 --> 01:49:10,100
Beat her.

1151
01:49:12,210 --> 01:49:14,040
Give her the whip. Give it all to her!

1152
01:49:15,810 --> 01:49:18,160
Platt, you come here and you beat her now!

1153
01:49:21,140 --> 01:49:22,210
Platt!

1154
01:49:25,120 --> 01:49:26,130
Come here!

1155
01:49:28,110 --> 01:49:30,030
I'd rather it you, Platt.

1156
01:49:31,150 --> 01:49:32,390
Strike her.

1157
01:49:33,840 --> 01:49:35,010
Strike her.

1158
01:49:57,520 --> 01:49:59,090
He pantomimes.

1159
01:49:59,940 --> 01:50:01,800
There ain't barely a welt on her.

1160
01:50:02,790 --> 01:50:04,820
That's what your niggers make of yah;

1161
01:50:05,260 --> 01:50:06,970
a fool fer the takin'.

1162
01:50:11,880 --> 01:50:13,960
Strike her, Platt! Strike her.

1163
01:50:31,060 --> 01:50:32,570
Yah will strike her.

1164
01:50:32,600 --> 01:50:34,910
Yah will strike her until her flesh is rent...

1165
01:50:34,910 --> 01:50:36,290
and meat and blood flow equal,

1166
01:50:36,290 --> 01:50:38,790
or I will kill every nigger in my sight!

1167
01:50:39,200 --> 01:50:42,100
Do you understand me? Strike her!

1168
01:50:42,100 --> 01:50:43,610
Strike her!

1169
01:51:27,070 --> 01:51:29,580
Until I say no more! I ain't said nothing!

1170
01:51:35,910 --> 01:51:36,630
Give me the whip!

1171
01:51:36,630 --> 01:51:37,480
Give it!

1172
01:51:39,750 --> 01:51:40,760
Give me the whip!

1173
01:51:41,870 --> 01:51:42,930
Get up!

1174
01:52:02,640 --> 01:52:03,980
Thou devil!

1175
01:52:06,980 --> 01:52:08,430
Sooner or later,

1176
01:52:09,100 --> 01:52:12,070
somewhere in the course of eternal justice

1177
01:52:12,070 --> 01:52:14,190
thou shalt answer for this sin!

1178
01:52:19,810 --> 01:52:22,660
Sin? There is no sin.

1179
01:52:24,460 --> 01:52:26,760
A man does how he pleases with his property.

1180
01:52:33,140 --> 01:52:36,260
At the moment, Platt, I am of great pleasure.

1181
01:52:36,780 --> 01:52:37,760
You be goddamn careful

1182
01:52:37,760 --> 01:52:40,370
I don't want to come lightenin' my mood no further.

1183
01:54:58,740 --> 01:54:59,970
Master Bass,

1184
01:55:01,080 --> 01:55:03,730
I want to ask you what part of the country you come from?

1185
01:55:05,310 --> 01:55:06,790
No part of this land.

1186
01:55:08,070 --> 01:55:09,390
Originate from Canada.

1187
01:55:10,890 --> 01:55:12,390
Now guess where that is.

1188
01:55:12,720 --> 01:55:14,590
Oh, I know where Canada is.

1189
01:55:15,520 --> 01:55:17,160
I have been there myself.

1190
01:55:22,250 --> 01:55:23,750
Montreal and

1191
01:55:24,250 --> 01:55:27,220
Kingston and Queenston and a great many places.

1192
01:55:27,240 --> 01:55:29,020
Well traveled for a slave.

1193
01:55:29,480 --> 01:55:30,850
How came you here?

1194
01:55:32,560 --> 01:55:34,090
Master Bass,

1195
01:55:36,540 --> 01:55:39,640
if justice had been done I never would have been here.

1196
01:55:44,820 --> 01:55:45,970
How's this?

1197
01:55:47,240 --> 01:55:48,340
Tell me all.

1198
01:55:53,660 --> 01:55:55,250
I am afraid to tell you.

1199
01:55:57,410 --> 01:56:00,270
Every word you speak is a profound secret.

1200
01:56:08,320 --> 01:56:09,540
Your story,

1201
01:56:10,620 --> 01:56:13,720
it is amazing, and in no good way.

1202
01:56:18,890 --> 01:56:20,580
Do you believe, sir,

1203
01:56:20,800 --> 01:56:22,760
in justice as you have said?

1204
01:56:23,550 --> 01:56:24,920
I do.

1205
01:56:25,510 --> 01:56:28,530
That slavery is an evil that should befall none?

1206
01:56:32,040 --> 01:56:35,200
- I believe so. - If you truly do,

1207
01:56:37,660 --> 01:56:39,120
then, I ask...

1208
01:56:39,800 --> 01:56:41,190
I beg...

1209
01:56:43,500 --> 01:56:45,970
that you write my friends in the north,

1210
01:56:46,670 --> 01:56:48,980
acquainting them with my situation,

1211
01:56:50,780 --> 01:56:52,920
and beseeching them to forward

1212
01:56:53,520 --> 01:56:54,870
free papers.

1213
01:57:00,020 --> 01:57:01,250
It would be...

1214
01:57:04,690 --> 01:57:07,190
an unspeakable happiness,

1215
01:57:09,110 --> 01:57:10,850
to see my wife

1216
01:57:13,880 --> 01:57:15,780
and my family again.

1217
01:57:21,920 --> 01:57:24,950
I've traveled this country for the best part of twenty years.

1218
01:57:26,160 --> 01:57:28,260
My freedom is everything.

1219
01:57:29,120 --> 01:57:31,040
The fact that I can walk out of here tomorrow

1220
01:57:31,050 --> 01:57:33,160
brings me great pleasure.

1221
01:57:35,950 --> 01:57:38,050
My life doesn't mean much to anyone,

1222
01:57:39,560 --> 01:57:42,970
but seems yours might mean a lot to a whole lot of people.

1223
01:57:44,960 --> 01:57:46,650
But what you ask me,

1224
01:57:46,970 --> 01:57:49,610
Sir, scares me.

1225
01:57:51,810 --> 01:57:55,110
And I must say, I am afraid.

1226
01:57:55,650 --> 01:57:57,640
Not just for you, but for me.

1227
01:58:07,140 --> 01:58:09,040
I will write your letter, sir,

1228
01:58:09,910 --> 01:58:11,650
and if it brings you your freedom,

1229
01:58:11,650 --> 01:58:12,850
it will be more than a pleasure,

1230
01:58:12,850 --> 01:58:14,220
it will be my duty.

1231
01:58:14,550 --> 01:58:17,570
Now, would you kindly hand me those shingles?

1232
02:00:52,120 --> 02:00:55,560
Platt? Where is the boy called Platt?

1233
02:00:59,040 --> 02:01:00,270
Come here, boy.

1234
02:01:22,680 --> 02:01:24,170
Your name is Platt, is it?

1235
02:01:26,080 --> 02:01:27,220
Yes, sir.

1236
02:01:28,220 --> 02:01:29,360
Do you know that man?

1237
02:01:47,370 --> 02:01:48,840
Mr. Parker?

1238
02:01:49,600 --> 02:01:51,080
Say again?

1239
02:01:53,090 --> 02:01:54,680
Mr. Parker?

1240
02:01:55,650 --> 02:01:58,360
That man received a letter compiling many accusations.

1241
02:01:58,420 --> 02:01:59,770
You look me in the eye,

1242
02:02:00,940 --> 02:02:02,560
and on your life you answer me truthfully:

1243
02:02:02,560 --> 02:02:04,310
have you any other name than Platt?

1244
02:02:04,310 --> 02:02:07,960
- Solomon Northup is my name. - Sheriff, what's all this?

1245
02:02:07,960 --> 02:02:10,770
- It's official business. - My nigga, my business.

1246
02:02:10,770 --> 02:02:12,410
Your business waits.

1247
02:02:12,800 --> 02:02:14,140
- Tell me of your family. - Platt.

1248
02:02:14,140 --> 02:02:15,790
I have a wife and two children.

1249
02:02:15,790 --> 02:02:17,280
- What the hell? - What were your children's names?

1250
02:02:17,280 --> 02:02:19,640
- Margaret and Alonzo. - And your wife's name before her marriage?

1251
02:02:19,640 --> 02:02:21,740
Anne Hampton. I am who I say.

1252
02:02:21,750 --> 02:02:23,290
Where are you going, Platt?

1253
02:02:24,000 --> 02:02:26,210
- Who authorized you to interfere with my property? - My authority.

1254
02:02:26,210 --> 02:02:28,570
Platt, you come back here! Platt!

1255
02:02:29,100 --> 02:02:30,380
You come back here, boy!

1256
02:02:34,330 --> 02:02:37,350
You will unhand him. Platt is my nigger!

1257
02:02:37,350 --> 02:02:39,730
- He is Mr. Solomon Northup! - You say,

1258
02:02:39,730 --> 02:02:42,470
you come here, unfamiliar to me and make claims.

1259
02:02:42,470 --> 02:02:44,170
We got no doubts. The man is Solomon Northup.

1260
02:02:44,170 --> 02:02:46,830
To hell he is! He's my nigger, and I'll fight you for him!

1261
02:02:46,830 --> 02:02:47,920
As is your right.

1262
02:02:47,920 --> 02:02:50,320
As it will be my pleasure to bankrupt you in the courts.

1263
02:02:50,320 --> 02:02:52,830
Your decision. Unhand him!

1264
02:02:53,880 --> 02:02:55,610
I know you had some hand in this plan.

1265
02:02:55,610 --> 02:02:56,580
I'm gonna get to the bottom of it.

1266
02:02:56,580 --> 02:02:57,810
It ain't no mine.

1267
02:02:57,810 --> 02:02:59,390
I paid good money for this nigga!

1268
02:02:59,390 --> 02:03:00,950
The courthouse got papers to prove it!

1269
02:03:00,960 --> 02:03:02,930
And we got papers proving he is free!

1270
02:03:02,930 --> 02:03:05,200
I own you! You belong to me! You hear me with that?

1271
02:03:05,210 --> 02:03:06,040
Unhand him!

1272
02:03:06,040 --> 02:03:08,340
The court will start to cast you back by sundown!

1273
02:03:08,720 --> 02:03:11,660
- Platt! - Get my horse, Treach.

1274
02:03:21,160 --> 02:03:22,800
Get away from him, Pats!

1275
02:03:24,010 --> 02:03:27,280
- I'll be seeing you real soon. - Solomon, we need to make haste.

1276
02:03:29,190 --> 02:03:31,770
- No. - Solomon!

1277
02:05:08,920 --> 02:05:10,780
I apologize

1278
02:05:13,140 --> 02:05:14,910
for my appearance.

1279
02:05:17,710 --> 02:05:19,560
But I have had

1280
02:05:20,690 --> 02:05:22,160
a difficult time

1281
02:05:23,670 --> 02:05:26,140
these past several years.

1282
02:05:31,130 --> 02:05:32,560
Margaret?

1283
02:05:38,250 --> 02:05:39,470
Alonzo?

1284
02:06:11,160 --> 02:06:12,270
Who is this?

1285
02:06:13,840 --> 02:06:15,490
He's my husband.

1286
02:06:17,340 --> 02:06:18,600
Husband.

1287
02:06:19,270 --> 02:06:22,460
It is very good to meet you, sir.

1288
02:06:24,500 --> 02:06:26,690
We have much acquainting to do.

1289
02:06:26,750 --> 02:06:28,140
Yes, sir.

1290
02:06:29,800 --> 02:06:31,090
And this

1291
02:06:31,320 --> 02:06:33,120
is your grandson.

1292
02:06:34,220 --> 02:06:36,940
Solomon Northup Staunton.

1293
02:06:47,730 --> 02:06:48,990
Solomon.

1294
02:06:59,190 --> 02:07:00,760
Forgive me.

1295
02:07:04,660 --> 02:07:07,950
There is nothing to forgive.

